From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Graham Ollis <plicease@cpan.org>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:15:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Take the environment from environ, since Open Watcom
 passes main() none

Open Watcom's startup (clibl.lib(cmain086)) calls main(argc, argv) with
argc in AX and argv in CX:BX and no third argument, so Perl 3's env
parameter is whatever lies in the caller's stack slots. Perl compares it
with environ, finds them different, sets environ[0] to null (emptying
the environment of every child process, so PATH and COMSPEC are lost),
and builds %ENV from the garbage. In the development build that garbage
happened to end at once, so %ENV was always empty; in other link
layouts it pointed at unmapped memory, and a script that mentioned eval
(which makes Perl initialise %ENV whether or not it is used) hung in
index() on 0xFF bytes. Microsoft C passed the environment to main(), so
the historical port never saw this (docs/M1-REPORT.md).

main() now uses environ under __WATCOMC__.
---
 perly.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/perly.c b/perly.c
--- a/perly.c
+++ b/perly.c
@@ -98,6 +98,10 @@
     char *validarg = "";
 #endif
 
+#ifdef __WATCOMC__
+    env = environ;	/* Open Watcom passes main() no environment */
+#endif
+
 #ifdef SETUID_SCRIPTS_ARE_SECURE_NOW
 #ifdef IAMSUID
 #undef IAMSUID
